Let $a$, $N$ and $	heta$ be real numbers with $N \ge 0$ and $|	heta| \le \pi / 2$. Then the series $\sum_{
u=0}^{\infty}  inom{N}{
u} \sin((a + 2
u)	heta)$ converges unconditionally to $2^N (\cos 	heta)^N \sin((a + N)	heta)$. Here $ inom{N}{
u} = N(N-1)\cdots(N-
u+1)/
u!$ is the generalized binomial coefficient, and $2^N$ and $(\cos 	heta)^N$ are real powers.
